;; expect: reject
;; why: `Symbol.concat` constrains the ELEMENTS of its argument, not the tag of
;; the argument itself: every element has to be a symbol, and 2 is not. A tag
;; lattice cannot state that, so with `carp-ct-types` as the backend this case is
;; missed; the products of `carp-ct-sub` hold it. It was the second `gap` in this
;; corpus to close.
(defmacro joined-name [] (Symbol.concat (list (quote prefix) 2)))
